-- Counterfactual search, evolutionary variant: when the space is too
-- big to enumerate.
--
-- counterfactual.kim enumerates: 4 levers × 2 listed options each. An
-- enterprise is not like that — hundreds of levers, continuous levels,
-- interventions nobody put on a menu. Enumeration dies combinatorially,
-- and worse: THE MENU ITSELF is the limitation, because the best move
-- may be one no options list contains.
--
-- So invert the roles. The model PROPOSES interventions — free
-- invention, seeded by the case and the incumbent plan — and the same
-- three-layer discipline holds the search:
--
--   kernel (certainty 1)   the baseline seed (best enumerated single
--                          change), and the invariant: a proposal is
--                          schema-structured, so "touches only mutable
--                          levers" stays a CHECKABLE fact even over
--                          free generation
--   explore (free)         plausibility screens and the tournament
--                          against the incumbent — judged, excluded
--                          from θ
--   verdict (live)         ONE memoized cross-family judgment on the
--                          final incumbent
--
-- Evolution starts from a defensible answer and must beat it to replace
-- it: if every proposal fails the gates, you still commit the
-- enumerated baseline. gen is deliberately NOT memoized — mutation
-- needs diversity; determinism would freeze the search.
--
-- The invoice does not grow with generations × children: one θ factor,
-- whether 6 proposals were tried or 6,000. That is the property that
-- scales to the enterprise case.
--
--   kimiya run counterfactual_evolve.kim
--   kimiya run counterfactual_evolve.kim generations=5 children=4

param generations: num = 3
param children: num = 2

pool A = "llama3.1:8b"
pool B = "gemma2:9b"
pool C = "mistral:7b"

use python "bizlib.py"

schema Proposal:
    factor: text
    change: text
    rationale: text

context k_plaus:
    domain     = "whether a business intervention is a plausible route to a stated outcome"
    preserve   = [causal_direction, constraint_respect, magnitude]
    allow_loss = [phrasing, ordering]

b := observe file("business.json")
check b.exists
biz := parse_biz(b.text)

-- Kernel seed: the search must beat this to matter.
incumbent := seed_intervention(biz)
rejected := 0

explore:
    forall g in range(generations):
        forall i in range(children):
            p := gen<Proposal>("Invent ONE business intervention that is NOT limited to any preset options. Case: " + summary(biz) + " Current best plan: " + incumbent + " Name the factor you change (must be one of: " + mutable_names(biz) + "), the concrete change, and a one-line rationale.") by A
            if check(is_mutable(p.factor, biz)):
                cand := describe_prop(p, biz)
                if judge<3,2/3> (cand |= "a plausible route from the current result to the expected result, within the immutable constraints") under k_plaus panel [B, C]:
                    if judge<3,2/3> (cand |= "a more promising route to the expected result than this plan: " + incumbent) under k_plaus panel [B, C]:
                        incumbent := cand
            else:
                rejected := rejected + 1

print "kernel-rejected proposals: " + str(rejected)
check len(incumbent) > 0

-- The verdict: fresh, outside explore, counted once, reusable across runs.
if memo judge<5,4/5> (incumbent |= "would plausibly move the business from the current result to the expected result") under k_plaus panel [B, C]:
    commit(incumbent)
else:
    abstain
